# fable5-crossmodel-dualjudge — cross-model panel + DUAL judge (Shadman's default, 2026-07).
#
# Diversity of THOUGHT (three model families answer blind) AND diversity of JUDGMENT (two model
# families adjudicate), with Fable 5 as the accountable synthesizer/orchestrator.
#
#   panel: Fable 5 + Opus 4.8 + GPT-5.5   (blind)
#   judge: Fable 5  AND  GPT-5.5          (run_dual_judge.sh — both, in parallel, blind)
#   synth: Fable 5                        (writes the final answer, grounded in BOTH discernments)
#
# Rationale: GPT-5.5 is much cheaper than Fable, so the workhorse panelist/judge roles lean on the
# cheaper frontier models (Opus 4.8, GPT-5.5) while Fable — the frontier model — is reserved for the
# accountable synthesis. Never drop GPT-5.5 from the panel (that's the fable5-duo anti-pattern).
#
# Presets assign DEFAULTS (:=), so any var you export explicitly still wins.
: "${FUSION_PANEL:=fable5,opus4.8,gpt5.5}"
: "${FUSION_JUDGES:=fable5,gpt5.5}"    # plural → run_dual_judge.sh runs both; synthesizer reads both
: "${FUSION_JUDGE:=fable5}"           # kept for single-judge fallback if codex is unavailable
: "${FUSION_SYNTH:=fable5}"
: "${FUSION_CLAUDE_MODEL:=claude-fable-5}"
: "${FUSION_OPUS_MODEL:=opus}"
: "${CODEX_PANELIST_MODEL:=gpt-5.5}"
: "${JUDGE_MODEL:=gpt-5.5}"
